From: masterxq <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] lockscreen: translate the PIN labels in the greeter
Description:
 The lock screen is loaded by the greeter of kscreenlocker, whose QML
 context translates i18n() calls in its own domain kscreenlocker_greet.
 The labels of the keypad ("Enter PIN", "Wrong PIN") are translated
 in the domain of this shell package and stayed untranslated. Name the
 domain, as the lock screen of the desktop shell does.
Author: masterxq
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-28
---
diff --git a/shell/contents/lockscreen/LockScreenState.qml b/shell/contents/lockscreen/LockScreenState.qml
index 88d6f945a..f5fa84435 100644
--- a/shell/contents/lockscreen/LockScreenState.qml
+++ b/shell/contents/lockscreen/LockScreenState.qml
@@ -82,8 +82,9 @@ QtObject {
     property bool isKeyboardMode: false
 
     property string pinLabel: enterPinLabel
-    readonly property string enterPinLabel: i18n("Enter PIN")
-    readonly property string wrongPinLabel: i18n("Wrong PIN")
+    // the lock screen runs in the greeter of kscreenlocker, whose default translation domain is its own
+    readonly property string enterPinLabel: i18nd("plasma_shell_org.kde.plasma.phone", "Enter PIN")
+    readonly property string wrongPinLabel: i18nd("plasma_shell_org.kde.plasma.phone", "Wrong PIN")
 
     signal reset()
     signal unlockSucceeded()
